When the standard REST API isn't enough, expose your own:

```apex
@RestResource(urlMapping='/orders/*')
global with sharing class OrderApi {
  @HttpPost global static Id create(OrderRequest body) { … }
}
```

- Endpoints live at `/services/apexrest/...` and need an authenticated caller.
- Validate input, return clear errors with the right status (`RestContext.response.statusCode = 400`).
- Make operations **idempotent** where possible: retries shouldn't create duplicates (use an external Id).
- Version your URL mappings (`/v1/orders`) so you can change them later.
